{"abstract":"The densest subgraph problem is a classic problem in combinatorial optimisation. Graphs with low maximum subgraph density are often called “uniformly sparse”, leading to algorithms parameterised by this density. However, in reality, the sparsity of a graph is not necessarily uniform. This calls for a formally well-defined, fine-grained notion of density. Danisch, Chan, and Sozio propose a definition for local density that assigns to each vertex v a value ρ*(v). This local density is a generalisation of the maximum subgraph density of a graph. I.e., if ρ(G) is the subgraph density of a finite graph G, then ρ(G) equals the maximum local density ρ*(v) over vertices v in G. They present a Frank-Wolfe-based algorithm to approximate the local density of each vertex with no theoretical (asymptotic) guarantees. We provide an extensive study of this local density measure. Just as with (global) maximum subgraph density, we show that there is a dual relation between the local out-degrees and the minimum out-degree orientations of the graph. We introduce the definition of the local out-degree g*(v) of a vertex v, and show it to be equal to the local density ρ*(v). We consider the local out-degree to be conceptually simpler, shorter to define, and easier to compute. Using the local out-degree we show a previously unknown fact: that existing algorithms already dynamically approximate the local density for each vertex with polylogarithmic update time. Next, we provide the first distributed algorithms that compute the local density with provable guarantees: given any ε such that ε−1 ∈ O(poly n), we show a deterministic distributed algorithm in the LOCAL model where, after O(ε−2 log2 n) rounds, every vertex v outputs a (1 + ε)-approximation of their local density ρ*(v). In CONGEST, we show a deterministic distributed algorithm that requires poly(log n, ε−1) · 2O(√log n) rounds, which is sublinear in n. As a corollary, we obtain the first deterministic algorithm running in a sublinear number of rounds for (1 + ε)-approximate densest subgraph detection in the CONGEST model.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797877"],"event":{"end":"2025-03-07","place":"Jena, de","start":"2025-03-04","title":"42<sup>nd</sup> International Symposium on Theoretical Aspects of Computer Science","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Distributed graph algorithms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"local density and its distributed approximation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.STACS.2025.25","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-797877","identifier":[{"id":"85219585583","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1eca754d-0215-43fd-809b-3599ae4dbb75"],"keyword":["Distributed graph algorithms","Graph density approximation","Graph density computation","Network analysis theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C7F096324F07548BC93ED92A091355BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.STACS.2025.25","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/394246497/LIPIcs.STACS.2025.25.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander Bjørn","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c49eca57-bd53-46e3-886a-700b7f04954d","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","name_org":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn","orcid":"0000-0002-9486-9115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.stacs.2025.25","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 42nd International Symposium on Theoretical Aspects of Computer Science (STACS 2025)","volume":"327"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219585583"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1eca754d-0215-43fd-809b-3599ae4dbb75"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Local Density and Its Distributed Approximation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797877","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Given a plane geometric graph G on n vertices, we want to augment it so that given parity constraints of the vertex degrees are met. In other words, given a subset R of the vertices, we are interested in a plane geometric supergraph G′ such that exactly the vertices of R have odd degree in G′\\G. We show that the question of whether such a supergraph exists can be decided in polynomial time for two interesting cases. First, when the vertices are in convex position, we present a linear-time algorithm. Building on this insight, we solve the case when G is a plane geometric path in O(nlogn) time. This solves an open problem posed by Catana, Olaverri, Tejel, and Urrutia (Appl. Math. Comput. 2020).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","Kleist, Linda","Parada, Irene","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798480"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-21","place":"Gozd Martuljek, si","start":"2024-06-19","title":"50th International Workshop on Graph-Theoretic Concepts in Computer Science","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Parada, Irene"],"country":["Germany","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Catalonia","University of Potsdam"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"augmenting plane straight line graphs to meet parity constraints","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85218444363","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798480","identifier":[{"id":"85218444363","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f4884bdd-c2ad-408a-a088-3afb4e870457"],"keyword":["Augmentation problems","Convex geometric graphs","Geometric paths","Parity constraints","Plane geometric graphs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2B46C187F20415FE6FD2CA191FA6DD2A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of potsdam","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Potsdam","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"polytechnic university of catalonia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Catalonia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c49eca57-bd53-46e3-886a-700b7f04954d","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","orcid":"0000-0002-9486-9115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Linda","key":"kleistpau","last":"Kleist","name":"Kleist, Linda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"paradapau","last":"Parada","name":"Parada, Irene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-75409-8_9","eisbn":["9783031754098"],"isbn":["9783031754081"],"pages":"121-135","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"50th International Workshop on Graph-Theoretic Concepts in Computer Science","volume":"14760"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218444363"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f4884bdd-c2ad-408a-a088-3afb4e870457"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Augmenting Plane Straight-Line Graphs to Meet Parity Constraints","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798480","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Union volume estimation is a classical algorithmic problem. Given a family of objects O1,...,On ⊂ Rd, we want to approximate the volume of their union. In the special case where all objects are boxes (also called hyperrectangles) this is known as Klee's measure problem. The state-of-the-art (1 + ∈)-approximation algorithm [Karp, Luby, Madras '89] for union volume estimation as well as Klee's measure problem in constant dimension d uses a total of O(n/∈2) queries of three types: (i) determine the volume of Oi; (ii) sample a point uniformly at random from Oi; and (iii) ask whether a given point is contained in Oi.  First, we show that if an algorithm learns about the objects only through these types of queries, then Ω(n/∈2) queries are necessary. In this sense, the complexity of [Karp, Luby, Madras '89] is optimal. Our lower bound holds even if the objects are equiponderous axis-aligned polygons in R2, if the containment query allows arbitrary (not necessarily sampled) points, and if the algorithm can spend arbitrary time and space examining the query responses. Second, we provide a more efficient approximation algorithm for Klee's measure problem, which improves the running time from O(n/∈2) to O((n+ 1/∈2) · logO(d)(n)). We circumvent our lower bound by exploiting the geometry of boxes in various ways: (1) We sort the boxes into classes of similar shapes after inspecting their corner coordinates. (2) With orthogonal range searching, we show how to sample points from the union of boxes in each class, and how to merge samples from different classes. (3) We bound the amount of wasted work by arguing that most pairs of classes have a small intersection.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bringmann, Karl","Larsen, Kasper Green","Nusser, André","Rotenberg, Eva","Wang, Yanheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827458"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-27","place":"Kanazawa, jp","start":"2025-06-23","title":"41st International Symposium on Computational Geometry","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Saarland University","Université Côte d’Azur"],"keyword":["Approximation","Query complexity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"approximating klee s measure problem and a lower bound for union volume estimation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.25","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827458","identifier":[{"id":"105009600223","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2df3caa0-2029-41f0-9f5b-0322a3faaa6c"],"keyword":["Approximation","Query complexity","Union of objects","Volume of union"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-DE9E9F1298F719DE982E6193272D8D00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/407890884/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.25.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.25","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"université côte d azur","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Côte d’Azur","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"bringmannpau","last":"Bringmann","name":"Bringmann, Karl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper Green","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Kasper Green","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"André","key":"nusserpau","last":"Nusser","name":"Nusser, André","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanheng","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yanheng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2025.25","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 41st International Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2025)","volume":"332"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009600223"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2df3caa0-2029-41f0-9f5b-0322a3faaa6c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Approximating Klee's Measure Problem and a Lower Bound for Union Volume Estimation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827458","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We cluster a set of trajectories T using subtrajectories of T . We require for a clustering C that any two subtrajectories (T [a, b], T [c, d]) in a cluster have disjoint intervals [a, b] and [c, d]. Clustering quality may be measured by the number of clusters, the number of vertices of T that are absent from the clustering, and by the Fréchet distance between subtrajectories in a cluster. A Δ-cluster of T is a cluster P of subtrajectories of T with a centre P ∈ P, where all subtrajectories in P have Fréchet distance at most Δ to P. Buchin, Buchin, Gudmundsson, Löffler and Luo present two O(n2 + nml)-time algorithms: SC(max, l, Δ, T) computes a single Δ-cluster where P has at least l vertices and maximises the cardinality m of P. SC(m, max, Δ, T) computes a single Δ-cluster where P has cardinality m and maximises the complexity l of P. In this paper, which is a mixture of algorithms engineering and theoretical insights, we use such maximum-cardinality clusters in a greedy clustering algorithm. We first provide an efficient implementation of SC(max, l, Δ, T) and SC(m, max, Δ, T) that significantly outperforms previous implementations. Next, we use these functions as a subroutine in a greedy clustering algorithm, which performs well when compared to existing subtrajectory clustering algorithms on real-world data. Finally, we observe that, for fixed Δ and T, these two functions always output a point on the Pareto front of some bivariate function θ(l,m). We design a new algorithm PSC(Δ, T) that in O(n2 log4 n) time computes a 2-approximation of this Pareto front. This yields a broader set of candidate clusters, with comparable quality to the output of the previous functions. We show that using PSC(Δ, T) as a subroutine improves the clustering quality and performance even further.","author_count":4,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Ost, Lara","Rotenberg, Eva","Rutschmann, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827671"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-27","place":"Kanazawa, jp","start":"2025-06-23","title":"41st International Symposium on Computational Geometry","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Vienna"],"keyword":["Fréchet distance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient greedy discrete subtrajectory clustering","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.78","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827671","identifier":[{"id":"105009601919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6da0a5b3-b687-41e3-8b73-a9e2148a9bc7"],"keyword":["Algorithms engineering","Fréchet distance","Subtrajectory clustering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-91DBA9AE5A24E8F077645BF5CD5121E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/407891983/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.78.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.78","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Vienna","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"Van Der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","name_org":"Van Der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lara","key":"ostpau","last":"Ost","name":"Ost, Lara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"rutschmannpau","last":"Rutschmann","locid":"11f18e5e-e42b-47ad-856a-e23469be187c","name":"Rutschmann, Daniel","orcid":"0009-0005-6838-2628","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2025.78","issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 41st International Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2025)","volume":"332"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009601919"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6da0a5b3-b687-41e3-8b73-a9e2148a9bc7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Efficient Greedy Discrete Subtrajectory Clustering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827671","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We present a deterministic fully-dynamic data structure for maintaining information about the cut-vertices in a graph; i.e. the vertices whose removal would disconnect the graph. Our data structure supports insertion and deletion of edges, as well as queries to whether a pair of connected vertices are either biconnected, or can be separated by a cutvertex, and in the latter case we support access to separating cutvertices. All update operations are supported in amortized O(log2 n log2 log n) time, and queries take worst-case O(log n log2 log n) time. Note that these time bounds match the current best for deterministic dynamic connectivity up to log log n factors.  The previous best algorithm for biconnectivity had an update time of O(log4 n log log n) by Thorup [STOC'00], based on the O(log5 n) data structure by Holm, de Lichtenberg, and Thorup [STOC'98]. We obtain our improved running time by a series of reductions from the original problem into well-defined data structure problems. While we do indeed apply the well-known techniques for improving running time of two-edge connectivity [STOC'00, SODA'18], surprisingly, these techniques alone do not lead to an update time of Õ(log³ n), let alone the Õ(log2 n) we give as a final result.  Our contributions include a formally defined transient expose operation, which can be thought of as a cheaper read-only expose operation on a top tree. For each vertex in the graph, we maintain a data structure over its neighbors, and in this data structure we apply biasing (twice) to save an Õ(log n) factor (twice, so two Õ(log n) factors). One of these biasing techniques is a new, simple biased disjoint sets data structure, which may be of independent interest. Moreover, in this neighborhood data structure, we facilitate that the vertex can select two VIP neighbors that get special treatment, corresponding to its potentially two neighbors on an exposed path, improving an otherwise log n-time operation down to constant time. It is this combination of VIP neighbors with the transient expose operation that saves an Õ(log n)-factor from another bottleneck. Combining these technical contributions with the well-known techniques for two-edge connectivity [STOC'00, SODA'18], we obtain the desired update times of O(log2 n log2 log n). The near-linear query time follows directly from the usage of transient expose.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","Nadara, Wojciech","Rotenberg, Eva","Sokołowski, Marek"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827490"],"event":{"end":"2025-06-27","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2025-06-23","title":"57<sup>th</sup> Annual ACM Symposium on Theory of Computing","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Informatics","University of Warsaw"],"keyword":["Dynamic","Top trees"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fully dynamic biconnectivity in õ log000000000002 n time","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3717823.3718270","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827490","identifier":[{"id":"105009856873","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-382ba646-160b-43c2-b5b7-e9bca974c78f"],"keyword":["Biconnectivity","Cut-vertex","Dynamic","Top trees"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-16599FF2013476A93E30F3F3F2AC150B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3717823.3718270","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/407893724/3717823.3718270.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pl","key":"university of warsaw","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warsaw","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for informatics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Informatics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wojciech","key":"nadarapau","last":"Nadara","name":"Nadara, Wojciech","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marek","key":"sokołowskipau","last":"Sokołowski","name":"Sokołowski, Marek","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3717823.3718270","eisbn":["798400715105/25/06"],"pages":"156-165","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 57th Annual ACM Symposium on Theory of Computing (STOC '25)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009856873"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-382ba646-160b-43c2-b5b7-e9bca974c78f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fully Dynamic Biconnectivity in Õ(log2 n) Time","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827490","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We consider the following variant of the edge-augmentation problem: Given a k-edge-connected graph with no loops or multiple edges, find a smallest edge set in the complement whose addition to G results in a (k+1)-edge-connected graph. We establish the following dichotomy for this problem: If the complement of G contains a matching covering all vertices of G-degree k (and possibly more), then the complement also contains a matching whose addition to G results in a (k+1)-edge-connected graph. A smallest matching which augments the minimum degree can be found, in polynomial time, by Edmonds' matching algorithm, but it need not augment the edge-connectivity. Indeed, it is NP-hard to find a smallest edge-connectivity augmenting edge set, by a result of Tibor Jordán. On the other hand, if the complement of G contains no matching covering all vertices of G-degree k, then the complement has a minimum degree augmenting path system consisting of paths of length 1 or 2. Again we can find such a path system with as few edges as possible by Edmonds' matching algorithm. We can, in polynomial time, modify it to an edge-connectivity augmenting path system of paths of length 1 or 2 with the same number of edges, and this time it yields a smallest edge-connectivity augmenting set of edges. Combining these results, we conclude that a smallest edge-connectivity augmenting edge set in the complement of a k-regular, k-edge-connected simple graph has size n-m(G), where n is the number of vertices of G, and (m(G) is the size of a maximum matching in the complement of G. Another corollary is that the complement of every simple noncomplete graph G with n vertices has a set of at most 2n/3 edges whose addition to G results in a graph of larger edge-connectivity, with equality holding if and only the complement of G is a disjoint union of 3-cycles.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Kasper Skov","Rotenberg, Eva","Thomassen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789525"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thomassen, Carsten"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"edge connectivity augmentation of simple graphs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386891768/accepted_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789525","identifier":[{"id":"85215441687","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fcedf69d-5517-497e-90ed-a8cf52a9ad33"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AAE0F699D63E2AE000280886A0B5F509"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386891768/accepted_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper Skov","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"ec2b7952-5b5a-441a-98f8-fe75492b7531","name":"Johansen, Kasper Skov","orcid":"0009-0005-3859-1226","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"88ab66ea-2b88-44e7-88f2-b8b883cf3ec0","name":"Thomassen, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-0670-4079","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/23m1574245","issn":["08954801","10957146"],"issn_org":["08954801"],"issue":"1","journal":"SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics","pages":"163-169","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215441687"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fcedf69d-5517-497e-90ed-a8cf52a9ad33"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Edge-Connectivity Augmentation of Simple Graphs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789525","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"EU’s program, der siden 2007 har støttet de bedste forskningsprojekter i Europa, er potentielt i fare. Hvis pengene i stedet går til projekter ud fra vurderet markedspotentiale, vil det koste på EU’s konkurrenceevne","author_count":42,"contributors":["Eriksen, Janus Juul","Simonsen, Kristina Bakkær","Koksbang, Sofie Marie","Alatraktchi, Fatima Alzahra’a","Albrechtsen, Nicolai","Laurine Albris, Sofie","Andersen, Lau Møller","Arbøll, Troels Pank","Autzen, Anton","Bjerre, Cecilie","Bjerva, Johannes","Bjørk, Anders","Damgaard, Rune Busk","Ellersgaard, Christoph","Eriksen, Christoffer Basse","Golovchenko, Yevgeniy","Hansen, Niels Christian","Hauptmann, Aviaja","Høyland-Kroghsbo, Nina Molin","Ørnsbjerg Jensen, Kirsten Marie","Kruse Jensen, Louise","Jønsson, Alexandra Brandt Ryborg","Kjærgaard, Morten","Kristoffersen, Emil Laust","Larsen, Matthew","Li, Elizabeth","Linding, Stine","Meaidi, Amani","Munk, Patrick","Munksgaard, Rasmus","Wullum Nielsen, Mathias","Kellberg Nielsen, Trine","Pearson, Sarah","Pultz, Sabina","Rotenberg, Eva","Rønholt, Stine","Skovmøller, Amalie","Stahl, Rune Møller","Sylow, Lykke","Thomsen, Torsten Bøgh","Uusimäki, Elisa","Zetterberg-Nielsen, Simona"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797503"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Nordic"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Greenland"],"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Moesgaard Museum"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danske politiker