ern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-00bda344-6374-4736-b315-6c4dd7f47514"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Danske politikere må forsvare EU’s succesprogram for grundforskning","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797503","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Fredman proposed in 1976 the following algorithmic problem: Given are a ground set X, some partial order P over X, and some comparison oracle OL that specifies a linear order L over X that extends P. A query to OL has as input distinct x,x‘ ϵ X and outputs whether x <L x’ or vice versa. If we denote by e (P ) the number of linear orders that extend P, then it follows from basic information theory that log e (P ) is a worst-case lower bound on the number of queries needed to output the sorted order of X. Fredman did not specify in what form the partial order is given. Haeupler, Hladík, Iacono, Rozhon, Tarjan, and Tětek (’24) propose to assume as input a directed acyclic graph, G, with m edges and n = |X| vertices. Denote by PG the partial order induced by G. Their algorithmic performance is measured in running time and the number of queries used, where they use Θ( m + n + log e (PG)) time and Θ(log e (PG)) queries to output X in its sorted order. Their algorithm is worst-case optimal, both in terms of running time and queries. Their analysis relies upon sophisticated counting arguments using entropy, recursively defined sets defined over the run of their algorithm, and vertices in the graph that they identify as bottlenecks for sorting. We do away with sophistication. We show that when the input is a directed acyclic graph then the problem admits a simple solution using Θ(m + n + log e (PG)) time and Θ(log e (PG)) queries. Especially our proofs are much simpler as we avoid the usage of advanced charging arguments, and instead rely upon two observations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva","Rutschmann, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808368"],"event":{"end":"2025-01-15","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2025-01-13","title":"2025 Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simpler optimal sorting from a directed acyclic graph","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85217060260","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808368","identifier":[{"id":"85217060260","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3d66b65d-ef25-417c-9800-f0527214f3f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-2209E8248F3C5EED836E7C28C0CF7DF6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"rutschmannpau","last":"Rutschmann","locid":"11f18e5e-e42b-47ad-856a-e23469be187c","name":"Rutschmann, Daniel","orcid":"0009-0005-6838-2628","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611978315","eisbn":["9781611978315"],"pages":"350-355","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2025 Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms (SOSA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217060260"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3d66b65d-ef25-417c-9800-f0527214f3f1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simpler Optimal Sorting from a Directed Acyclic Graph","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808368","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The Fréchet distance is a popular distance measure between curves P and Q. Conditional lower bounds prohibit (1 + ε)-approximate Fréchet distance computations in strongly subquadratic time, even when preprocessing P using any polynomial amount of time and space. As a consequence, the Fréchet distance has been studied under realistic input assumptions, for example, assuming both curves are c-packed. In this paper, we study c-packed curves in Euclidean space Rd and in general geodesic metrics X. In Rd, we provide a nearly-linear time static algorithm for computing the (1 + ε)-approximate continuous Fréchet distance between c-packed curves. Our algorithm has a linear dependence on the dimension d, as opposed to previous algorithms which have an exponential dependence on d. In general geodesic metric spaces X, little was previously known. We provide the first data structure, and thereby the first algorithm, under this model. Given a c-packed input curve P with n vertices, we preprocess it in O(nlog n) time, so that given a query containing a constant ε and a curve Q with m vertices, we can return a (1 + ε)-approximation of the discrete Fréchet distance between P and Q in time polylogarithmic in n and linear in m, 1/ε, and the realism parameter c. Finally, we show several extensions to our data structure; to support dynamic extend/truncate updates on P, to answer map matching queries, and to answer Hausdorff distance queries.","author_count":5,"contributors":["van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva","Wong, Sampson"],"cuid":["S02-093.67-785366"],"event":{"end":"2024-12-11","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2024-12-08","title":"35th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation, ISAAC 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Approximation algorithms","Data structures","Fréchet distance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data structures for approximate fréchet distance for realistic curves","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2024.56","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.67-785366","identifier":[{"id":"85213043187","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f21df303-58b5-4b02-bf8a-5b0c19a7b2ff","ku-322b1095-1ac4-4822-9d5e-3af4882c90af"],"keyword":["Approximation algorithms","Data structures","Fréchet distance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BE3F2E0AEB0198895DC8DED09A70A357"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386878226/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2024.56.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/415880203/Data_Structures_for_Approximate_Fr_chet_Distance.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ISAAC.2024.56","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sampson","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","locid":"4e6706ad-b288-430a-9755-267c0f491761","name":"Wong, Sampson","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Julian","key":"mestrepedh","last":"Mestre","name":"Mestre, Julian","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anthony","key":"wirthpedh","last":"Wirth","name":"Wirth, Anthony","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.isaac.2024.56","eisbn":["9783959773546"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 35th International Symposium on Algorithms and Computation (ISAAC 2024)","volume":"322"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85213043187"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f21df303-58b5-4b02-bf8a-5b0c19a7b2ff","ku-322b1095-1ac4-4822-9d5e-3af4882c90af"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data Structures for Approximate Fréchet Distance for Realistic Curves","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.67-785366","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We present a data structure that, given a graph G of n vertices and m edges, and a suitable pair of nested r-divisions of G, preprocesses G in O(m+n) time and handles any series of edge-deletions in O(m) total time while answering queries to pairwise biconnectivity in worst-case O(1) time. In case the vertices are not biconnected, the data structure can return a cutvertex separating them in worst-case O(1) time. As an immediate consequence, this gives optimal amortized decremental biconnectivity, 2-edge connectivity, and connectivity for large classes of graphs, including planar graphs and other minor free graphs.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-785351"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["2 connectivity","Dynamic graphs","Graph minors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"good i r i divisions imply optimal amortized decremental biconnectivity","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00224-024-10181-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-785351","identifier":[{"id":"85197952501","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a6997c79-a361-47ca-baca-251c5813c63b","ku-d6fba80b-fe31-435b-ad1f-680f153b3bd9"],"keyword":["2-connectivity","Dynamic graphs","Graph minors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-33C6491DC386884B2075636EACF104A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/413849893/s00224_024_10181_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00224-024-10181-z","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of English, Germanic and Romance Studies","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00224-024-10181-z","issn":["14324350","14330490"],"issn_org":["14324350"],"journal":"Theory of Computing Systems","pages":"1014-1048","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Theory of Computing Systems","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197952501"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a6997c79-a361-47ca-baca-251c5813c63b","ku-d6fba80b-fe31-435b-ad1f-680f153b3bd9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Good r-divisions Imply Optimal Amortized Decremental Biconnectivity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785351","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this work we study local computation with advice: the goal is to solve a graph problem Π with a distributed algorithm in f (Δ) communication rounds, for some function f that only depends on the maximum degree Δ of the graph, and the key question is how many bits of advice per node are needed. Our main results are: (1) Any locally checkable labeling problem (LCL) can be solved in graphs with sub-exponential growth with only 1 bit of advice per node. Moreover, we can make the set of nodes that carry advice bits arbitrarily sparse. (2) The assumption of sub-exponential growth is necessary: assuming the Exponential-Time Hypothesis (ETH), there are LCLs that cannot be solved in general with any constant number of bits per node. (3) In any graph we can find an almost-balanced orientation (indegrees and outdegrees differ by at most one) with 1 bit of advice per node, and again we can make the advice arbitrarily sparse. (4) As a corollary, we can also compress an arbitrary subset of edges so that a node of degree d stores only d/2 + 2 bits, and we can decompress it locally, in f(Δ) rounds. (5) In any graph of maximum degree Δ, we can find a Δ-coloring (if it exists) with 1 bit of advice per node, and again, we can make the advice arbitrarily sparse. (6) In any 3-colorable graph, we can find a 3-coloring with 1 bit of advice per node. Here, it remains open whether we can make the advice arbitrarily sparse.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Balliu, Alkida","Brandt, Sebastian","Kuhn, Fabian","Nowicki, Krzysztof","Olivetti, Dennis","Rotenberg, Eva","Suomela, Jukka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-746676"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","France","Germany","Italy"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Gran Sasso Science Institute","Helmholtz Center for Information Security","Pathway.com","University of Freiburg"],"keyword":["Locality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"brief announcement local advice and local decompression","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3662158.3662805","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-746676","identifier":[{"id":"85199024577","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-751d38cf-608f-4324-a8d4-805f676df830"],"keyword":["Distributed advice","Distributed decompression","Locality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7B10C32ED5D6B6770060AD5FABC030E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/364222246/3662158.3662805.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3662158.3662805","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"gran sasso science institute","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Gran Sasso Science Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"helmholtz center for information security","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Center for Information Security","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"pathway com","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Pathway.com","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alkida","key":"balliupau","last":"Balliu","name":"Balliu, Alkida","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Sebastian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabian","key":"kuhnpau","last":"Kuhn","name":"Kuhn, Fabian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Krzysztof","key":"nowickipau","last":"Nowicki","name":"Nowicki, Krzysztof","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis","key":"olivettipau","last":"Olivetti","name":"Olivetti, Dennis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jukka","key":"suomelapau","last":"Suomela","name":"Suomela, Jukka","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3662158.3662805","eisbn":["9798400706684/24/06"],"pages":"117-120","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 43rd ACM Symposium on Principles of Distributed Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199024577"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-751d38cf-608f-4324-a8d4-805f676df830"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Brief Announcement: Local Advice and Local Decompression","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-746676","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Dynamic Time Warping (DTW) distance is a popular similarity measure for polygonal curves (i.e., sequences of points). It finds many theoretical and practical applications, especially for temporal data, and is known to be a robust, outlier-insensitive alternative to the Fréchet distance. For static curves of at most n points, the DTW distance can be computed in O(n2) time in constant dimension. This tightly matches a SETH-based lower bound, even for curves in R 1. In this work, we study dynamic algorithms for the DTW distance. Here, the goal is to design a data structure that can be efficiently updated to accommodate local changes to one or both curves, such as inserting or deleting vertices and, after each operation, reports the updated DTW distance. We give such a data structure with update and query time O(n1.5 log n), where n is the maximum length of the curves. As our main result, we prove that our data structure is conditionally optimal, up to subpolynomial factors. More precisely, we prove that, already for curves in R 1, there is no dynamic algorithm to maintain the DTW distance with update and query time O(n1.5−δ) for any constant δ > 0, unless the Negative-k-Clique Hypothesis fails. In fact, we give matching upper and lower bounds for various trade-offs between update and query time, even in cases where the lengths of the curves differ.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bringmann, Karl","Fischer, Nick","van der Hoog, Ivor","Kipouridis, Evangelos","Kociumaka, Tomasz","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798367"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Informatics","Saarland University","Weizmann Institute of Science"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic dynamic time warping","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.10","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798367","identifier":[{"id":"85188335646","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cb0a154d-4e43-44c0-848d-afd2f4ceee4a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-315DFB7F8A07998CF641AD50BA1306EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.10","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/388065972/1.9781611977912.10.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"saarland university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Saarland University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"weizmann institute of science","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Weizmann Institute of Science","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for informatics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Informatics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl","key":"bringmannpau","last":"Bringmann","name":"Bringmann, Karl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nick","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Nick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Evangelos","key":"kipouridispau","last":"Kipouridis","name":"Kipouridis, Evangelos","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasz","key":"kociumakapau","last":"Kociumaka","name":"Kociumaka, Tomasz","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611977912.10","eisbn":["9781611977912"],"pages":"208-242","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms (SODA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188335646"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cb0a154d-4e43-44c0-848d-afd2f4ceee4a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dynamic Dynamic Time Warping","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798367","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We study dynamic planar graphs with n vertices, subject to edge deletion, edge contraction, edge insertion across a face, and the splitting of a vertex in specified corners. We dynamically maintain a combinatorial embedding of such a planar graph, subject to connectivity and 2-vertex-connectivity (biconnectivity) queries between pairs of vertices. Whenever a query pair is connected and not biconnected, we find the first and last cut vertex separating them. Additionally, we allow local changes to the embedding by flipping the embedding of a subgraph that is connected by at most two vertices to the rest of the graph. We support all queries and updates in deterministic, worst-case, O(log2 n) time, using an O(n)-sized data structure.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809370"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"worst case deterministic fully dynamic biconnectivity in changeable planar embeddings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20382/jocg.v15.i2.a7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809370","identifier":[{"id":"85218757013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2a2fa953-2ed2-4a23-be7b-95fc7bf0a258"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1BF1C309BAC00F6D8E9F4A0CB755AC82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20382/jocg.v15.i2.a7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446091935/WORST-CASE_DETERMINISTIC_FULLY-DYNAMIC_BICONNECTIVITY.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.20382/jocg.v15.i2.a7","issn":["1920180X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Computational Geometry","pages":"222-257","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computational Geometry","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218757013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2a2fa953-2ed2-4a23-be7b-95fc7bf0a258"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Worst-case deterministic fully-dynamic biconnectivity in changeable planar embeddings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809370","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We give improved algorithms for maintaining edge-orientations of a fully-dynamic graph, such that the maximum out-degree is bounded. On one hand, we show how to orient the edges such that maximum outdegree is proportional to the arboricity α of the graph, in, either, an amortised update time of O(log2 nlog α), or a worst-case update time of O(log3 nlog α). On the other hand, motivated by applications including dynamic maximal matching, we obtain a different trade-off. Namely, the improved update time of either O(log nlog α), amortised, or O(log2 nlog α), worst-case, for the problem of maintaining an edge-orientation with at most O(α + log n) out-edges per vertex. Finally, all of our algorithms naturally limit the recourse to be polylogarithmic in n and α. Our algorithms adapt to the current arboricity of the graph, and yield improvements over previous work: Firstly, we obtain deterministic algorithms for maintaining a (1 + ε) approximation of the maximum subgraph density, ρ, of the dynamic graph. Our algorithms have update times of O(ε−6 log3 nlog ρ) worst-case, and O(ε−4 log2 nlog ρ) amortised, respectively. We may output a subgraph H of the input graph where its density is a (1 + ε) approximation of the maximum subgraph density in time linear in the size of the subgraph. These algorithms have improved update time compared to the O(ε−6 log4 n) algorithm by Sawlani and Wang from STOC 2020. Secondly, we obtain an O(ε−6 log3 nlog α) worst-case update time algorithm for maintaining a (1 + ε)OPT + 2 approximation of the optimal out-orientation of a graph with adaptive arboricity α, improving the O(ε−6α2 log3 n) algorithm by Christiansen and Rotenberg from ICALP 2022. This yields the first worst-case polylogarithmic dynamic algorithm for decomposing into O(α) forests. Thirdly, we obtain arboricity-adaptive fully-dynamic deterministic algorithms for a variety of problems including maximal matching, ∆ + 1 colouring, and matrix vector multiplication. All update times are worst-case O(α + log2 nlog α), where α is the current arboricity of the graph. For the maximal matching problem, the state-of-the-art deterministic algorithms by Kopelowitz, Krauthgamer, Porat, and Solomon from ICALP 2014 runs in time O(α2 + log2 n), and by Neiman and Solomon from STOC 2013 runs in time O(√m). We give improved running times whenever the arboricity α ∈ ω(log n√log log n).","author_count":7,"contributors":["Chekuri, Chandra","Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","Holm, Jacob","van der Hoog, Ivor","Quanrud, Kent","Rotenberg, Eva","Schwiegelshohn, Chris"],"cuid":["S02-091.11-735409"],"event":{"end":"2024-01-10","place":"Alexandria, us","start":"2024-01-07","title":"35th Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Purdue University","University of Illinois","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adaptive out orientations with applications","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.110","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.11-735409","identifier":[{"id":"85186221629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9feeed21-7b5f-4d77-b783-eca0d2666bd8","ku-e1e930d6-3670-4f86-884b-1dafdb69bfcc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DA2F11A50246EC1D44C30F85DF34BC6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/393864837/Adaptive_Out_Orientations_with_Applications.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/356869976/1.9781611977912.110.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977912.110","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of illinois","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of illinois at urbana champaign","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"purdue university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Purdue University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Eur