{"abstract":"The top tree data structure is an important and fundamental tool in dynamic graph algorithms. Top trees have existed for decades, and today serve as an ingredient in many state-of-the-art algorithms for dynamic graphs. In this work, we give a new direct proof of the existence of top trees, facilitating simpler and more direct implementations of top trees, based on ideas from splay trees. This result hinges on new insights into the structure of top trees, and in particular the structure of each root path in a top tree. In amortized analysis, our top trees match the asymptotic bounds of the state of the art.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","Ryhl, Alice"],"cuid":["S02-087.63-725030"],"event":{"end":"2023-01-25","place":"Florence, it","start":"2023-01-23","title":"SIAM Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"splay top trees","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977585.ch28","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.63-725030","identifier":[{"id":"85183916247","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4dc0ad37-3bc6-41ad-98db-60e1c4594da4","ku-6147a391-fb1a-49e9-899e-df9f4c3143b9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-D605C0FB33B0874F8CBBC5C5ED4E3D20"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977585.ch28","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/383441847/Splay_Top_Trees.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/315531232/1.9781611977585.ch28.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice","key":"ryhlpau","last":"Ryhl","name":"Ryhl, Alice","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Telikepalli","key":"kavithapedh","last":"Kavitha","name":"Kavitha, Telikepalli","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kurt","key":"mehlhornpedh","last":"Mehlhorn","name":"Mehlhorn, Kurt","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611977585.ch28","eisbn":["9781611977585"],"pages":"305-331","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2023 Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms (SOSA)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183916247"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4dc0ad37-3bc6-41ad-98db-60e1c4594da4","ku-6147a391-fb1a-49e9-899e-df9f4c3143b9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Splay Top Trees","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.63-725030","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We study dynamic planar graphs with n vertices, subject to edge deletion, edge contraction, edge insertion across a face, and the splitting of a vertex in specified corners. We dynamically maintain a combinatorial embedding of such a planar graph, subject to connectivity and 2-vertex-connectivity (biconnectivity) queries between pairs of vertices. Whenever a query pair is connected and not biconnected, we find the first and last cutvertex separating them. Additionally, we allow local changes to the embedding by flipping the embedding of a subgraph that is connected by at most two vertices to the rest of the graph. We support all queries and updates in deterministic, worst-case, O(log2 n) time, using an O(n)-sized data structure.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S02-089.76-725097"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-15","place":"Dallas, us","start":"2023-06-12","title":"39th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","van der Hoog, Ivor"],"keyword":["Connectivity","Dynamic graphs","Planarity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"worst case deterministic fully dynamic biconnectivity in changeable planar embeddings","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.40","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Ivor van der Hoog and Eva Rotenberg: Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis”. Jacob Holm: Partially supported by the VILLUM Foundation grant 16582, “BARC”. Ivor van der Hoog: This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No 899987. Ivor van der Hoog and Eva Rotenberg: Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis”. Jacob Holm: Partially supported by the VILLUM Foundation grant 16582, “BARC”. Ivor van der Hoog: This project has received funding from the European Union's Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No 899987."],"id":"S02-089.76-725097","identifier":[{"id":"85163488881","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e966b063-67bc-4eb4-a2dd-c7889d16f6a3","ku-c911c64c-9a23-45ec-9781-570cd0f82267"],"keyword":["Connectivity","Dynamic graphs","Planarity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-263D21599E591ECA3CFFC0F6EA77A832"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/383441432/Worst_Case_Deterministic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/330154495/LIPIcs_SoCG_2023_40.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.40","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erin W.","key":"chamberspedh","last":"Chambers","name":"Chambers, Erin W.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joachim","key":"gudmundssonpedh","last":"Gudmundsson","name":"Gudmundsson, Joachim","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2023.40","eisbn":["9783959772730"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"39th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163488881"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e966b063-67bc-4eb4-a2dd-c7889d16f6a3","ku-c911c64c-9a23-45ec-9781-570cd0f82267"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Worst-Case Deterministic Fully-Dynamic Biconnectivity in Changeable Planar Embeddings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.76-725097","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we give a new, efficient algorithm for computing curve skeletons, based on local separators. Our efficiency stems from a multilevel approach, where we solve small problems across levels of detail and combine these in order to quickly obtain a skeleton. We do this in a highly modular fashion, ensuring complete flexibility in adapting the algorithm for specific types of input or for otherwise targeting specific applications.  Separator based skeletonization was first proposed by Bærentzen and Rotenberg in [ACM Tran. Graphics'21], showing high quality output at the cost of running times which become prohibitive for large inputs. Our new approach retains the high quality output, and applicability to any spatially embedded graph, while being orders of magnitude faster for all practical purposes. We test our skeletonization algorithm for efficiency and quality in practice, comparing it to local separator skeletonization on the University of Groningen Skeletonization Benchmark [Telea'16].","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bærentzen, Jakob Andreas","Christensen, Rasmus Emil","Gæde, Emil Toftegaard","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683441"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-15","place":"Dallas, us","start":"2023-06-12","title":"39th International Symposium on Computational Geometry","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bærentzen, Jakob Andreas","Gæde, Emil Toftegaard","Rotenberg, Eva"],"keyword":["Algorithm engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multilevel skeletonization using local separators","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.13","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Emil Toftegaard Gæde and Eva Rotenberg: supported by Eva Rotenberg’s Carlsberg Foundation Young Researcher Fellowship CF21-0302 - “Graph Algorithms with Geometric Applications”. J. Andreas Bærentzen: Partially supported by the Villum Foundation through Villum Investigator Project InnoTop. Emil Toftegaard Gæde and Eva Rotenberg: supported by Eva Rotenberg's Carlsberg Foundation Young Researcher Fellowship CF21-0302 - “Graph Algorithms with Geometric Applications”. J. Andreas Bærentzen: Partially supported by the Villum Foundation through Villum Investigator Project InnoTop."],"id":"S01-000.00-683441","identifier":[{"id":"85163427927","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9730b6ba-cfe1-4bfa-9d42-1dfef1bcb177"],"keyword":["Algorithm engineering","Curve skeletons","Experimentation and implementation","Multilevel algorithm","Shape skeletonization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D6BA3A503FA5C914E4E66AE96F49B589"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.13","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/330362907/LIPIcs_SoCG_2023_13.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. Andreas","key":"bærentzenpau","last":"B