{"abstract":"Coresets are among the most popular paradigms for summarizing data. In particular, there exist many high performance coresets for clustering problems such as k-means in both theory and practice. Curiously, there exists no work on comparing the quality of available k-means coresets. In this paper we perform such an evaluation. There currently is no algorithm known to measure the distortion of a candidate coreset. We provide some evidence as to why this might be computationally difficult. To complement this, we propose a benchmark for which we argue that computing coresets is challenging and which also allows us an easy (heuristic) evaluation of coresets. Using this benchmark and real-world data sets, we conduct an exhaustive evaluation of the most commonly used coreset algorithms from theory and practice.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Schwiegelshohn, Chris","Sheikh-Omar, Omar Ali"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-144498"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-09","place":"Berlin/Potsdam, de","start":"2022-09-05","title":"30th Annual European Symposium on Algorithms, ESA 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmark","Evaluation","coresets"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an empirical evaluation of k means coresets","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2022.84","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-144498","identifier":[{"id":"85137592857","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1a7213bb-78d9-4d78-96de-869681d7a381"],"keyword":["benchmark","coresets","evaluation","k-means coresets"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7ED6A6D9E4CC2BEA0B2F6A7C4AAE3854"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2022.84","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chris","key":"schwiegelshohnpau","last":"Schwiegelshohn","locid":"cf8db534-0678-466f-b731-351f7264004e","name":"Schwiegelshohn, Chris","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Omar Ali","key":"sheikhomarpau","last":"Sheikh-Omar","locid":"5cde819a-1c4b-4063-9787-0252964a41d0","name":"Sheikh-Omar, Omar Ali","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shiri","key":"chechikpedh","last":"Chechik","name":"Chechik, Shiri","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gonzalo","key":"navarropedh","last":"Navarro","name":"Navarro, Gonzalo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpedh","last":"Rotenberg","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Grzegorz","key":"hermanpedh","last":"Herman","name":"Herman, Grzegorz","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2022.84","eisbn":["9783959772471"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"30th Annual European Symposium on Algorithms, ESA 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137592857"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1a7213bb-78d9-4d78-96de-869681d7a381"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"An Empirical Evaluation of k-Means Coresets","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-144498","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The Fréchet distance is a well-studied similarity measure between curves that is widely used throughout computer science. Motivated by applications where curves stem from paths and walks on an underlying graph (such as a road network), we define and study the Fréchet distance for paths and walks on graphs. When provided with a distance oracle of G with O(1) query time, the classical quadratic-time dynamic program can compute the Fréchet distance between two walks P and Q in a graph G in O(|P |· |Q|) time. We show that there are situations where the graph structure helps with computing Fréchet distance: when the graph G is planar, we apply existing (approximate) distance oracles to compute a (1 + e)-approximation of the Fréchet distance between any shortest path P and any walk Q in O(|G| log |G|/ve + |P | + |Qe| ) time. We generalise this result to near-shortest paths, i.e. ?-straight paths, as we show how to compute a (1 + e)-approximation between a ?-straight path P and any walk Q in O(|G| log |G|/ve + |P | + ?|eQ| ) time. Our algorithmic results hold for both the strong and the weak discrete Fréchet distance over the shortest path metric in G. Finally, we show that additional assumptions on the input, such as our assumption on path straightness, are indeed necessary to obtain truly subquadratic running time. We provide a conditional lower bound showing that the Fréchet distance, or even its 1.01-approximation, between arbitrary paths in a weighted planar graph cannot be computed in O((|P | · |Q|)1-d) time for any d > 0 unless the Orthogonal Vector Hypothesis fails. For walks, this lower bound holds even when G is planar, unit-weight and has O(1) vertices.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Driemel, Anne","van der Hoog, Ivor","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-307521"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-10","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2022-06-07","title":"38<sup>th</sup> International Symposium on Computational Geometry","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Driemel, Anne"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bonn"],"keyword":["Complexity analysis","Fréchet","Graphs","Planar"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the discrete fréchet distance in a graph","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2022.36","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis”."],"id":"S01-000.00-307521","identifier":[{"id":"85134302958","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-09ba54b1-0e32-4b3b-b4fe-5540c63d91e6"],"keyword":["Complexity analysis","Fréchet","Graphs","Planar"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7E2E2F31B0F05414C48A1A14684769DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/283412664/LIPIcs_SoCG_2022_36.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2022.36","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"driemelpau","last":"Driemel","name":"Driemel, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ivor","key":"vanderhoogpau","last":"van der Hoog","locid":"572104ae-4bbf-426e-aebd-3455726726de","name":"van der Hoog, Ivor","orcid":"0009-0006-2624-0231","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"goaocpedh","last":"Goaoc","name":"Goaoc, Xavier","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kerberpedh","last":"Kerber","name":"Kerber, Michael","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2022.36","eisbn":["9783959772273"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 38<sup>th</sup> International Symposium on Computational Geometry"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134302958"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-09ba54b1-0e32-4b3b-b4fe-5540c63d91e6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"On the Discrete Fréchet Distance in a Graph","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-307521","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The arboricity α of a graph is the smallest number of forests necessary to cover its edges, and an arboricity decomposition of a graph is a decomposition of its edges into forests. The best near-linear time algorithm for arboricity decomposition guarantees at most α + 2 forests if the graph has arboricity α (Blumenstock and Fischer [12]). In this paper, we study arboricity decomposition for dynamic graphs, that is, graphs that are subject to insertions and deletions of edges. We give an algorithm that, provided the arboricity of the dynamic graph never exceeds α, maintains an α + 2 arboricity decomposition of the graph in poly(log n, α) update time, thus matching the number of forests currently obtainable in near-linear time for static (non-changing) graphs. Our construction goes via dynamic bounded out-degree orientations, and we present a fully-dynamic algorithm that explicitly orients the edges of the dynamic graph, such that no vertex has an out-degree exceeding ⌊(1 + ε)α⌋+ 2. Our algorithm is deterministic and has a worst-case update time of O(ε−6α2 log3 n). The state-of-the-art explicit, deterministic, worst-case algorithm for bounded out-degree orientations maintains a β · α + logβ n out-orientation in O(β2α2 + βα logβ n) time [30]. As a consequence, we get an algorithm that maintains an implicit vertex colouring with 4 · 2α colours, in amortised poly-log n update time, and with O(α log n) worst-case query time. Thus, at the expense of log n-factors in the update time, we improve on the number of colours from 2O(α) to O(2α) compared to the state-of-the-art for implicit dynamic colouring [27].","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364112"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-08","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2022-07-04","title":"49<sup>th</sup> EATCS International Conference on Automata, Languages, and Programming","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt"],"keyword":["Bounded arboricity","Data structures","Dynamic graphs","Graph colouring"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fully dynamic α 000000000002 arboricity decompositions and implicit colouring","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ICALP.2022.42","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding Aleksander B. G. Christiansen: Partially supported by the VILLUM Foundation grant 37507 “Efficient Recomputations for Changeful Problems”. Eva Rotenberg: Partially supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark grants 2020-2023 (9131-00044B) “Dynamic Network Analysis” and 2018-2021 (8021-00249B) “AlgoGraph”, and the VILLUM Foundation grant 37507 “Efficient Recomputations for Changeful Problems”."],"id":"S01-000.00-364112","identifier":[{"id":"85133419063","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c75421b9-95a5-4796-9082-0c4d2093f48b"],"keyword":["Bounded arboricity","Data structures","Dynamic graphs","Graph colouring"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-39F6D6139CBDF729B5EC81DFFC1C904E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/283413815/LIPIcs_ICALP_2022_42.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ICALP.2022.42","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander B.G.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c49eca57-bd53-46e3-886a-700b7f04954d","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","name_org":"Christiansen, Aleksander B.G.","orcid":"0000-0002-9486-9115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikolaj","key":"bojanczykpedh","last":"Bojanczyk","name":"Bojanczyk, Mikolaj","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Emanuela","key":"merellipedh","last":"Merelli","name":"Merelli, Emanuela","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David P.","key":"woodruffpedh","last":"Woodruff","name":"Woodruff, David P.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.icalp.2022.42","eisbn":["9783959772358"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 49<sup>th</sup> EATCS International Conference on Automata, Languages, and Programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133419063"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c75421b9-95a5-4796-9082-0c4d2093f48b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fully-Dynamic α + 2 Arboricity Decompositions and Implicit Colouring","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-364112","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A graph has arboricity α if its edges can be partitioned into α forests. The dynamic arboricity decomposition problem is to update a partitioning of the graph's edges into forests, as a graph undergoes insertions and deletions of edges. We present an algorithm for maintaining partitioning into α + 1 forests, provided the arboricity of the dynamic graph never exceeds α. Our algorithm has an update time of O(n3/4) when α is at most polylogarithmic in n. Similarly, the dynamic bounded out-orientation problem is to orient the edges of the graph such that the out-degree of each vertex is at all times bounded. For this problem, we give an algorithm that orients the edges such that the out-degree is at all times bounded by α + 1, with an update time of O (n5/7), when α is at most polylogarithmic in n. Here, the choice of α + 1 should be viewed in the light of the well-known lower bound by Brodal and Fagerberg which establishes that, for general graphs, maintaining only α out-edges would require linear update time. However, the lower bound by Brodal and Fagerberg is non-planar. In this paper, we give a lower bound showing that even for planar graphs, linear update time is needed in order to maintain an explicit three-out-orientation. For planar graphs, we show that the dynamic four forest decomposition and four-out-orientations, can be updated in O(n1/2) time.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","Thomassen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319280"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-26","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2022-08-22","title":"47<sup>th</sup> International Symposium on Mathematical Foundations of Computer Science","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bounded arboricity","Data structures","Dynamic graphs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on dynamic α 000000000001 arboricity decomposition and out orientation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2022.34","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319280","identifier":[{"id":"85137565588","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-317d8347-f54c-40a5-8ac8-ec9cd371ad80"],"keyword":["Bounded arboricity","Data structures","Dynamic graphs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-D3CAF5371316C7F68E843E77A7A2C342"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/296727662/LIPIcs_MFCS_2022_34.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2022.34","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksander B.G.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"c49eca57-bd53-46e3-886a-700b7f04954d","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander Bjørn Grodt","name_org":"Christiansen, Aleksander B.G.","orcid":"0000-0002-9486-9115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jacob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"88ab66ea-2b88-44e7-88f2-b8b883cf3ec0","name":"Thomassen, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-0670-4079","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.mfcs.2022.34","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","paperid":"34","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","volume":"241"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137565588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-317d8347-f54c-40a5-8ac8-ec9cd371ad80"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"On Dynamic α+ 1 Arboricity Decomposition and Out-Orientation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319280","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The classic string indexing problem is to preprocess a string S into a compact data structure that supports efficient subsequent pattern matching queries, that is, given a pattern string P, report all occurrences of P within S. In this paper, we study a basic and natural extension of string indexing called the string indexing for top-k close consecutive occurrences problem (SITCCO). Here, a consecutive occurrence is a pair (i,j), i<j, such that P occurs at positions i and j in S and there is no occurrence of P between i and j, and their distance is defined as j−i. Given a pattern P and a parameter k, the goal is to report the top-k consecutive occurrences of P in S of minimal distance. The challenge is to compactly represent S while supporting queries in time close to the length of P and k. We give three time-space trade-offs for the problem. Let n be the length of S, m the length of P, and ϵ∈(0,1]. Our first result achieves O(nlog⁡n) space and optimal query time of O(m+k). Our second and third results achieve linear space and query times either O(m+k1+ϵ) or O(m+klog1+ϵ⁡n). Along the way, we develop several techniques of independent interest, including a new translation of the problem into a line segment intersection problem and a new recursive clustering technique for trees.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bille, Philip","Gørtz, Inge Li","Pedersen, Max Rishøj","Rotenberg, Eva","Steiner, Teresa Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348744"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Steiner, Teresa Anna"],"keyword":["Consecutive occurrences","Pattern matching","String indexing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"string indexing for top k close consecutive occurrences","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2022.06.004","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank anonymous reviewers of an earlier draft of this paper for their insightful comments and suggestions for improvement. Philip Bille, Inge Li Gørtz, Max Pedersen and Eva Rotenberg were partially supported by the Danish Research Council grant Adaptive Compressed Computation (DFF-8021-002498)."],"id":"S01-000.00-348744","identifier":[{"id":"85132226484","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9413b021-ef93-4628-91c8-6a859efa65ec"],"keyword":["Consecutive occurrences","Pattern matching","String indexing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-376007606C70C3EB7F4BF52B4E6DCE42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/315530390/1_s2.0_S0304397522003565_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2022.06.004","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Philip","key":"billepau","last":"Bille","locid":"81ad6edf-aa11-47bc-adaf-227fe7e6963e","name":"Bille, Philip","orcid":"0000-0002-1120-5154","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge Li","key":"gørtzpau","last":"Gørtz","locid":"08da98e0-b1f4-492e-94e7-15083cc40701","name":"Gørtz, Inge Li","orcid":"0000-0002-8322-4952","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max Rishøj","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d88e8491-c512-4a0a-a6c3-41f61be01870","name":"Pedersen, Max Rishøj","orcid":"0000-0002-8850-6422","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa Anna","key":"steinerpau","last":"Steiner","locid":"229ad7cd-2c7d-417c-8333-01832e47680e","name":"Steiner, Teresa Anna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tcs.2022.06.004","issn":["03043975"],"journal":"Theoretical Computer Science","pages":"133-147","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Theoretical Computer Science","volume":"927"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132226484"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9413b021-ef93-4628-91c8-6a859efa65ec"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"String indexing for top-k close consecutive occurrences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-348744","year":"2022","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Motivated by a real-world vehicle routing application, we consider the maximum-weight independent set problem: Given a node-weighted graph, find a set of independent (mutually nonadjacent) nodes whose node-weight sum is maximum. Some of the graphs arising in the vehicle routing application are large, having hundreds of thousands of nodes and hundreds of millions of edges. To solve instances of this size, we develop a new local search algorithm, which is a metaheuristic based on the greedy randomized adaptive search (GRASP) framework. This algorithm, named METAMIS, uses a wider range of simple local search operations than previously described in the literature. We introduce data structures that make these operations efficient. A new variant of path-relinking is introduced to escape local optima and so is a new alternating augmenting-path local search move that improves algorithm performance. We compare an implementation of our algorithm with a state-of-the-art publicly available code on public benchmark sets, including some large instances. Our algorithm is, in general, competitive and outperforms this openly available code on large vehicle routing instances of the maximum weight independent set problem. We hope that our results will lead to even better maximum-weight independent set algorithms.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dong, Yuanyuan","Goldberg, Andrew V.","Noe, Alexander","Parotsidis, Nikos","Resende, Mauricio G.C.","Spaen, Quico"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515133"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-09","place":"Berlin/Potsdam, de","start":"2022-09-05","title":"30th Annual European Symposium on Algorithms, ESA 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amazon.com, Inc.","University of Washington"],"keyword":["GRASP","Heuristic","Local search","Maximum weight independent set","Metaheuristic","Path relinking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a local search algorithm for large maximum weight independent set problems","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2022.45","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-515133","identifier":[{"id":"85137571315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cbca0978-4690-4deb-84f7-3c73257c5aaf"],"keyword":["GRASP","heuristic","local search","maximum-weight independent set","metaheuristic","path-relinking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FB7EFFF760E165C5084A6FDE5426447C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320112727/A_Local_Search_Algorithm_for_Large_Maximum.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2022.45","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"amazon com inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Amazon.com, Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Yuanyuan","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Yuanyuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andrew V.","key":"goldbergpau","last":"Goldberg","name":"Goldberg, Andrew V.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alexander","key":"noepau","last":"Noe","name":"Noe, Alexander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nikos","key":"parotsidispau","last":"Parotsidis","locid":"34705be6-55af-4f91-86be-510199c83b9a","name":"Parotsidis, Nikos","orcid":"0000-0003-3888-7391","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Mauricio G.C.","key":"resendepau","last":"Resende","name":"Resende, Mauricio G.C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Quico","key":"spaenpau","last":"Spaen","name":"Spaen, Quico","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shiri","key":"chechikpedh","last":"Chechik","name":"Chechik, Shiri","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gonzalo","key":"navarropedh","last":"Navarro","name":"Navarro, Gonzalo","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpedh","last":"Rotenberg","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Grzegorz","key":"hermanpedh","last":"Herman","name":"Herman, Grzegorz","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2022.45","eisbn":["9783959772471"],"issn":["18688969"],"pages":"1-16","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"30th Annual European Symposium on Algorithms, ESA 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137571315"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cbca0978-4690-4deb-84f7-3c73257c5aaf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Local Search Algorithm for Large Maximum Weight Independent Set Problems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-515133","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A graph has arboricity α if its edges can be partitioned into α forests. The dynamic arboricity decomposition problem is to update a partitioning of the graph's edges into forests, as a graph undergoes insertions and deletions of edges. We present an algorithm for maintaining partitioning into α + 1 forests, provided the arboricity of the dynamic graph never exceeds α. Our algorithm has an update time of O(n3/4) when α is at most polylogarithmic in n. Similarly, the dynamic bounded out-orientation problem is to orient the edges of the graph such that the out-degree of each vertex is at all times bounded. For this problem, we give an algorithm that orients the edges such that the out-degree is at all times bounded by α + 1, with an update time of O (n5/7), when α is at most polylogarithmic in n. Here, the choice of α + 1 should be viewed in the light of the well-known lower bound by Brodal and Fagerberg which establishes that, for general graphs, maintaining only α out-edges would require linear update time. However, the lower bound by Brodal and Fagerberg is non-planar. In this paper, we give a lower bound showing that even for planar graphs, linear update time is needed in order to maintain an explicit three-out-orientation. For planar graphs, we show that the dynamic four forest decomposition and four-out-orientations, can be updated in O(n1/2) time.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Christiansen, Aleksander B.G.","Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","Thomassen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505284"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-26","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2022-08-22","title":"47th International Symposium on Mathematical Foundations of Computer Science, MFCS 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bounded arboricity","Data structures","Dynamic graphs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on dynamic α 000000000001 arboricity decomposition and out orientation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2022.34","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-505284","identifier":[{"id":"85137565588","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bb6513f7-3f50-4694-802d-84db1674ab25"],"keyword":["Dynamic graphs","bounded arboricity","data structures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-D3CAF5371316C7F68E843E77A7A2C342"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.MFCS.2022.34","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320114256/On_Dynamic_1_Arboricity_Decomposition.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Aleksander B.G.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Aleksander B.G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","name":"Thomassen, Carsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefan","key":"szeiderpedh","last":"Szeider","name":"Szeider, Stefan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert","key":"ganianpedh","last":"Ganian","name":"Ganian, Robert","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandra","key":"silvapedh","last":"Silva","name":"Silva, Alexandra","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.mfcs.2022.34","eisbn":["9783959772563"],"issn":["18688969"],"pages":"1-15","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"47th International Symposium on Mathematical Foundations of Computer Science, MFCS 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137565588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bb6513f7-3f50-4694-802d-84db1674ab25"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On Dynamic α+ 1 Arboricity Decomposition and Out-Orientation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505284","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We propose a new algorithm for curve skeleton computation that differs from previous algorithms by being based on the notion of local separators. The main benefits of this approach are that it is able to capture relatively fine details and that it works robustly on a range of shape representations. Specifically, our method works on shape representations that can be construed as spatially embedded graphs. Such representations include meshes, volumetric shapes, and graphs computed from point clouds. We describe a simple pipeline where geometric data are initially converted to a graph, optionally simplified, local separators are computed and selected, and finally a skeleton is constructed. We test our pipeline on polygonal meshes, volumetric shapes, and point clouds. Finally, we compare our results to other methods for skeletonization according to performance and quality.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bærentzen, Jakob Andreas","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-370164"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"skeletonization via local separators","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265674193/2007.03483.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-370164","identifier":[{"id":"85124100729","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-db3bafd6-9fc4-4d35-8813-ef14fee33c33"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B4392B82EF56821CD4C69C954303C8A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265674193/2007.03483.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"bærentzenpau","last":"Bærentzen","locid":"f0d1a57d-f173-4c59-87ad-b554b3678a8c","name":"Bærentzen, Jakob Andreas","name_org":"Bærentzen, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0003-2583-0660","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3459233","issn":["07300301","15577368"],"issn_org":["07300301"],"issue":"5","journal":"ACM Transactions on Graphics","paperid":"187","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Graphics","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124100729"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-db3bafd6-9fc4-4d35-8813-ef14fee33c33"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Skeletonization via Local Separators","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-370164","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
