t":"Rotenberg","locid":"00219c09-8417-495f-96ff-eb34884ad59c","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert","key":"krauthgamerpedh","last":"Krauthgamer","name":"Krauthgamer, Robert","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611974331.ch111","eisbn":["9781611974331"],"pages":"1631-1642","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Twenty-Seventh Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963612588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-293df5ab-4c64-4948-9a9e-0e8a008ec129"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The power of two choices with simple tabulation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418062","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The power of two choices is a classic paradigm for load balancing when assigning m balls to n bins. When placing a ball, we pick two bins according to two hash functions ho and h1, and place the ball in the least loaded bin. Assuming fully random hash functions, when m = O(n), Azar et al. [STOC'94] proved that the maximum load is lglgn + 0(1) with high probability. No such bound was known with a hash function implementable in constant time. In this paper, we investigate the power of two choices when the hash functions ho and h1 are implemented with simple tabulation, which is a very efficient hash function evaluated in constant time. Following their analysis of Cuckoo hashing [J.ACM'12], PǍtraşcu and Thorup claimed that the expected maximum load with simple tabulation is O(lglgn). This did not include any high probability guarantee, so the load balancing was not yet to be trusted. Here, we show that with simple tabulation, the maximum load is O(lglgn) with high probability, giving the first constant time hash function with this guarantee. We also give a concrete example where, unlike with fully random hashing, the maximum load is not bounded by lglgn + 0(l), or even (1 + o(l)) lglgn with high probability. Finally, we show that the expected maximum load is lglgn + 0(1), just like with fully random hashing.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dahlgaard, Søren","Knudsen, Mathias Baek Tejs","Rotenberg, Eva","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-306659"],"event":{"acronym":"SODA","end":"2016-01-12","place":"Arlington, us","start":"2016-01-10","title":"27th Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the power of two choices with simple tabulation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84963612588","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-306659","identifier":[{"id":"84963612588","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-06e11a87-4a31-474e-ba76-d8b20ba87d38"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-205B34BFF57A7B1D21D24BBF35381CDE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","name":"Dahlgaard, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Baek Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Mathias Baek Tejs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611974331.ch111","eisbn":["9781510819672"],"pages":"1631-1642","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"27th Annual ACM-SIAM Symposium on Discrete Algorithms, SODA 2016","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963612588"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-06e11a87-4a31-474e-ba76-d8b20ba87d38"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The power of two choices with simple tabulation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-306659","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We give a new data structure for the fully-dynamic minimum spanning forest problem in simple graphs. Edge updates are supported in O(log4 n/log logn) expected amortized time per operation, improving the O(log4 n) amortized bound of Holm et al. (STOC’98, JACM’01).We also provide a deterministic data structure with amortized update time O(log4 nlogloglogn/log logn). We assume the Word-RAM model with standard instructions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","Wulff-Nilsen, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-080.60-038004"],"event":{"acronym":"ESA","end":"2015-09-16","place":"Patras, gr","start":"2015-09-14","title":"23rd European Symposium on Algorithms","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"faster fully dynamic minimum spanning forest","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84945535380","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-080.60-038004","identifier":[{"id":"84945535380","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f39617f4-d209-41cd-8748-2ae0852667f6","ku-cc3e06b8-dd3e-4537-8aff-f7974abd7e18"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8041830A8EF190A6236F9260E8C8F430"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"wulffnilsenpau","last":"Wulff-Nilsen","locid":"10a26f7c-95c5-4716-ba80-32ad40ba4f07","name":"Wulff-Nilsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-3699-7821","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-48350-3_62","eisbn":["9783662483503"],"isbn":["9783662483497"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"742-753","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture notes in computer science","status":"p","subtitle":"23rd Annual European Symposium, Patras, Greece, September 14-16, 2015, Proceedings","title":"Algorithms - ESA 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84945535380"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f39617f4-d209-41cd-8748-2ae0852667f6","ku-cc3e06b8-dd3e-4537-8aff-f7974abd7e18"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Faster Fully-Dynamic minimum spanning forest","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.60-038004","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We present an algorithm to support the dynamic embedding in the plane of a dynamic graph. An edge can be inserted across a face between two vertices on the boundary (we call such a vertex pair linkable), and edges can be deleted. The planar embedding can also be changed locally by flipping components that are connected to the rest of the graph by at most two vertices. Given vertices u, v, linkable(u, v) decides whether u and v are linkable, and if so, returns a list of suggestions for the placement of (u, v) in the embedding. For non-linkable vertices u, v, we define a new query, one-flip-linkable(u, v) providing a suggestion for a flip that will make them linkable if one exists. We will support all updates and queries in O(log2 n) time. Our time bounds match those of Italiano et al. for a static (flipless) embedding of a dynamic graph. Our new algorithm is simpler, exploiting that the complement of a spanning tree of a connected plane graph is a spanning tree of the dual graph. The primal and dual trees are interpreted as having the same Euler tour, and a main idea of the new algorithm is an elegant interaction between top trees over the two trees via their common Euler tour.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva"],"cuid":["S02-092.21-034322"],"event":{"acronym":"STACS","end":"2015-03-07","place":"Garching, de","start":"2015-03-04","title":"32nd International Symposium on Theoretical Aspects of Computer Science","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Data structures","Dynamic graphs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic planar embeddings of dynamic graphs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.STACS.2015.434","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.21-034322","identifier":[{"id":"84923865134","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4d3eb867-2a3a-4e29-806f-1403916e6f92","ku-da72b790-dfb0-4a16-a5d3-42429c88a9a2"],"keyword":["Data structures","Dynamic graphs","Planar embeddings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DBB7CA07931AC40826FC5BA49A952175"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/137154561/31.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.STACS.2015.434","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ernst W.","key":"mayrpedh","last":"Mayr","name":"Mayr, Ernst W.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicolas","key":"ollingerpedh","last":"Ollinger","name":"Ollinger, Nicolas","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.stacs.2015.434","eisbn":["9783939897781"],"pages":"434-446","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl-Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik","publisher_org":"Schloss Dagstuhl--Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik","status":"p","title":"32nd Symposium on Theoretical Aspects of Computer Science (STACS 2015)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923865134"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4d3eb867-2a3a-4e29-806f-1403916e6f92","ku-da72b790-dfb0-4a16-a5d3-42429c88a9a2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamic planar embeddings of dynamic graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.21-034322","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We show how to represent a planar digraph in linear space so that reach ability queries can be answered in constant time. The data structure can be constructed in linear time. This representation of reach ability is thus optimal in both time and space, and has optimal construction time. The previous best solution used O(n log n) space for constant query time [Thorup FOCS'01].","author_count":3,"contributors":["Holm, Jacob","Rotenberg, Eva","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S02-088.42-034742"],"event":{"acronym":"FOCS","end":"2015-10-20","place":"Berkeley, California, us","start":"2015-10-18","title":"56th IEEE Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science, FOCS 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Data structures","Directed graphs","Planar graphs","Reachability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"planar reachability in linear space and constant time","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.5867v2.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-088.42-034742","identifier":[{"id":"84960364193","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5e46835e-74f0-43ab-beb7-ee20a601ecae","ku-a13cb0cb-b19a-4d0c-8779-89a883b72c0f"],"keyword":["Planar graphs","data structures","directed graphs","reachability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-14D673B1CBF4B41C849E3AC81AB8B89F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.5867v2.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"b9128f70-a478-4df0-9f6b-cc665f65976c","name":"Holm, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6997-9251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/focs.2015.30","eisbn":["9781467381918"],"issn":["15238288"],"pages":"370-389","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science. Annual Proceedings","status":"p","title":"2015 IEEE 56th Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science (FOCS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960364193"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5e46835e-74f0-43ab-beb7-ee20a601ecae","ku-a13cb0cb-b19a-4d0c-8779-89a883b72c0f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Planar Reachability in Linear Space and Constant Time","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.42-034742","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we analyze a hash function for k-partitioning a set into bins, obtaining strong concentration bounds for standard algorithms combining statistics from each bin. This generic method was originally introduced by Flajolet and Martin [FOCS'83] in order to save a factor Ω(k) of time per element over k independent samples when estimating the number of distinct elements in a data stream. It was also used in the widely used Hyper Log Log algorithm of Flajolet et al. [AOFA'97] and in large-scale machine learning by Li et al. [NIPS'12] for minwise estimation of set similarity. The main issue of k-partition, is that the contents of different bins may be highly correlated when using popular hash functions. This means that methods of analyzing the marginal distribution for a single bin do not apply. Here we show that a tabulation based hash function, mixed tabulation, does yield strong concentration bounds on the most popular applications of k-partitioning similar to those we would get using a truly random hash function. The analysis is very involved and implies several new results of independent interest for both simple and double tabulation, e.g. A simple and efficient construction for invertible bloom filters and uniform hashing on a given set.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dahlgaard, Soren","Knudsen, Mathias Baek Tejs","Rotenberg, Eva","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S02-090.51-033061"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-20","place":"Berkeley, California, us","start":"2015-10-18","title":"56th IEEE Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science, FOCS 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Concentration Bounds","Hashing","Peelability","Tabulation Hashing","Uniform Hashing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hashing for statistics over i k i partitions","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.7191v3.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-090.51-033061","identifier":[{"id":"84960345251","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-15df3d4a-547b-4fae-a798-31150e6169e8","ku-c6fe98db-37a3-4a4b-9312-81570a06b1f3"],"keyword":["Hashing","concentration bounds","constant moments","invertible bloom filters","joint distributions","k-partition","peelability","tabulation hashing","uniform hashing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB0443E7D87E7EA19439B3168EC3180C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"http://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.7191v3.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The APL Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"dahlgaardpau","last":"Dahlgaard","locid":"4788aa93-be24-420b-8767-e735d6dcc61d","name":"Dahlgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2925-746X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias Bæk Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"28c3a2af-0485-4bfb-83ba-e8a330c65b22","name":"Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs","orcid":"0000-0001-5308-9609","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/focs.2015.83","eisbn":["9781467381918"],"pages":"1292-1310","publisher":"IEEE Computer Society Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2015 IEEE 56th Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science, FOCS 2015","volume":"2015-December"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960345251"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-15df3d4a-547b-4fae-a798-31150e6169e8","ku-c6fe98db-37a3-4a4b-9312-81570a06b1f3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hashing for Statistics over K-Partitions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.51-033061","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Discrete linear transformations are important tools in information processing. Many such transforms are injective and therefore prime candidates for a physically reversible implementation into hardware. We present here reversible integer cosine transformations on n input integers. The resulting reversible circuit is able to perform both the forward transform and the inverse transform. The detailed structure of such a reversible design strongly depends on the odd prime factors of the determinant of the transform: whether those are of the form 2k ± 1 or of the form 2k ± 2l ± 1 or neither of these forms.","author_count":8,"contributors":["De Vos, Alexis","Burignat, Stephane","Gluck, Robert","Mogensen, Torben Agidius","Axelsen, Holger Bock","Thomsen, Michael K.","Rotenberg, Eva","Yokoyama, Tetsuo"],"cuid":["S02-092.65-034304"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["De Vos, Alexis"],"country":["Belgium","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ghent University","Nanzan University"],"keyword":["Reversible computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing garbage free reversible implementations of the integer cosine transform","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84910124118","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.65-034304","identifier":[{"id":"84910124118","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4c5fea92-bfd4-4a7f-aa80-91f40da8aa2b","ku-3608108f-8af7-4b47-9374-8495ce006715"],"keyword":["Garbage-free multiplication","Integer cosine transform","Reversible computa