{"abstract":"Recently, a reversible garbage-free 2 k ±1 constant-multiplier circuit was presented by Axelsen and Thomsen. This was the first construction of a garbage-free, reversible circuit for multiplication with non-trivial constants. At the time, the strength, that is, the range of constants obtainable by cascading these circuits, was unknown. In this paper, we show that there exist infinitely many constants we cannot multiply by using cascades of 2 k ±1-multipliers; in fact, there exist infinitely many primes we cannot multiply by. Using these results, we further provide an algorithm for determining whether one can multiply by a given constant using a cascade of 2 k ±1-multipliers, and for generating the minimal cascade of 2 k ±1-multipliers for an obtainable constant, giving a complete characterization of the problem. A table of minimal cascades for multiplying by small constants is provided for convenience.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rotenberg, Eva","Cranch, James","Thomsen, Michael K.","Axelsen, Holger Bock"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-371400"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-05","place":"Victoria, BC, ca","start":"2013-07-04","title":"5th International Conference on Reversible Computation","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Number theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strength of the reversible garbage free 000000000002 sup k sup 000000000001 multiplier","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84880704415","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-371400","identifier":[{"id":"84880704415","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-df82b5d7-8a3e-40ce-bde5-bea2f7d968fa"],"keyword":["Mersenne numbers","Number theory","constant multiplication","reversible circuit design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-D73B018D62341884A3680EB3F4DD7162"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms and Logic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"rotenbergpau","last":"Rotenberg","locid":"1a970eb9-57c6-4f5f-a453-117cbc7705ba","name":"Rotenberg, Eva","orcid":"0000-0001-5853-7909","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"cranchpau","last":"Cranch","name":"Cranch, James","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael K.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Michael K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger Bock","key":"axelsenpau","las